    "long_instructions": "A biologist predicted the weights of five different animals, and you’d like to calculate the mean squared error of their predictions to see how good or bad the predictions are.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. Import the `mean_squared_error` function.\r\n2. Compute the mean squared error for the biologist’s predictions, saving the resulting loss in a variable.\r\n3. Print the value of the loss.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nTo use `scikit-learn`’s mean squared error function, first import it with:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error\r\n```\r\nThen, call the function by passing in the actual values as the first argument and the predicted values as the second argument.\r\n",
